\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"daa59b694dbe4d3a8b3034cac7b22130635c3e88fe6cbe3736fcf33e5fa6edc2","event_uuid":"00a041cd-91c1-4f9d-8f9a-e4ced8ea8f44","position":{"commit_sha":"94caf428a16c1480c548418ee3006c43130830a4","position":"1785985843492954001-00a041cd-91c1-4f9d-8f9a-e4ced8ea8f44"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"},{"content_hash":"d4f50d23286a552e97e230d08974b57373bab855020957c929e202b700606946","event_uuid":"319d9ae6-eef4-4ac4-b224-63d5e8f161be","position":{"commit_sha":"1d1bbfcf4584117524571f2d875c0eb565ceea7c","position":"1785986862645986001-319d9ae6-eef4-4ac4-b224-63d5e8f161be"},"signature":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","signer_pubkey":"ssh-ed25519 AAAAC3NzaC1lZDI1NTE5AAAAIHe3p+OG3L79IIh99qRBEkAEXaU+VbeQcSfhIu4M2F8b rebar-bot joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com"}],"bridge_alerts":[],"claim_harness":null,"claim_remote_session":null,"claimed_session":null,"comments":[{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","body":"CLOSING EVIDENCE — all 7 children closed, all 5 epic ACs live-proven on Bedrock.\n\nAC1 (runaway detected DURING run, aborted, routed to verdict): c827 merged (Gerrit 1447, 125163c94d) + fd84. Four consecutive production captures during this session's own closes: aborts at 84, 158, 83, and 67 requests (vs the historical 240-request burnouts), each followed by bounded recovery delivering a real verdict. Two captures had max_consecutive_repeat=1 — rotating k-cycles the old adjacent metric was provably blind to (70bc); the windowed distinct-ratio (window 24, trip <=0.50) fired on all.\n\nAC2 (no mid-run tool-surface emptying / Bedrock toolConfig 400): e1b1 closed; the c827 guard raises BEFORE executing the repeated call and never empties the surface; zero Bedrock 400s across all live runs (exp_i/k/l + four gate closes).\n\nAC3 (every exhaustion/runaway leaves gate_error_v1 with repetition counters): 8b97 (render at raise_completion_workflow_failure) + 215f (diagnostic survives prelude failure; Gerrit 1448 merged 4792fac4b9). Live: the c827 close-failure sidecar carried full counters and drove the ed6d bug report directly from its diagnostic.\n\nAC4 (durable usage recording incl. loop-vs-breadth axis): aec1 closed — tool_calls + distinct + max_consecutive_repeat + distinct_ratio_window recorded by default; every WARNING line quoted above came from that instrumentation.\n\nAC5 (healthy breadth never truncated): test_healthy_run_past_flat_landing_threshold_is_never_aborted (Gerrit 1450 merged 9a27202837) — a 251-request high-novelty run lands naturally past the old 239 flat-landing threshold; the 94a3 and 215f closes also completed through the gate without truncation.\n\nEnd-to-end validation: 94a3-1323-3497-4f59 (the parallel session's stuck ticket, four prior exhaustions) closed + signed through the new gate without --force. Residual defect discovered while dogfooding filed as ed6d-5448-4ff6-4b8a (P1, discovered_from c827): one criterion's evidence-run exhaustion kills whole bounded recovery — plan written and signed, not a blocker for this epic's ACs.","timestamp":1785985843492954001}],"created_at":1785954507399157001,"creation_channel":"cli","deps":[{"link_uuid":"f268d7ff-3346-4819-a806-c68a91b34128","relation":"relates_to","target_id":"6c3e-67c6-eafa-45e7"}],"description":"## Context / Problem\n\nThe completion-verification close gate dies verdict-less when its agentic verify step falls into a tool-call loop: the step budget exhausts, the run surfaces a bare `LLMError` with `diagnostic: null`, and the only documented exit is `--force-close` (an unattested close). Four exhaustions on epic e369; three of four instrumented runs LOOPED, wasting 40-70% of each pathological run (measured on ticket c827-2a23-cd00-473e). Six prior attempts adjusted budgets or added reporting; none acted at the layer where the loop happens.\n\n## Approach\n\nFix the causal chain end to end, in dependency order. First give the repetition detector a signal that separates a k-cycle from healthy breadth (a windowed distinct-ratio produced in `usage_log._repetition_summary` — the existing headline metric is provably inverted on real traces). Independently, replace the provider-broken forced-landing primitive: the `tool_step_limit` empty-filter rewrite in `src/rebar/llm/agent_call.py` causes a Bedrock/Anthropic 400 (`toolConfig` must be defined while history holds `toolUse` blocks — live-proven) — keep tools advertised and steer with synthetic tool results instead. Make bounded recovery reachable for a step-budget exhaustion (`CompletionAgentStep.run` currently catches only `UnretryableOutputError`), and surface the already-computed repetition diagnostic in the `gate_error_v1` sidecar. Then wire the detector to ACT during the run: a typed runaway error classified ahead of the provider-outage fallback in `interpret_failure`, routed into the shipped bounded recovery + tool-free finalizer so the verdict is built from fresh per-criterion evidence, never the poisoned history. Finally, record per-run request/tool-call usage durably by default so the gate can be tuned from data. This fits the problem because every piece wires or repairs a mechanism that already exists and was measured failing — nothing parallel is introduced.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n\n- [x] a runaway tool-call cycle in the completion gate's verify step is detected DURING the run, aborted at that point, and routed to a verdict built from fresh per-criterion evidence — never a bare `LLMError` with `diagnostic: null`; checked by the actuator child's end-to-end test\n- [x] no code path empties the advertised tool surface mid-run after a tool call has occurred, so the Bedrock/Anthropic toolConfig 400 cannot recur; checked by a regression test asserting tool definitions persist for the whole run\n- [x] every budget exhaustion or runaway leaves an operator-actionable diagnostic (a `gate_error_v1` sidecar carrying the repetition counters) distinguishing \"it looped\" from \"it ran out of room\"; checked by the diagnostic child's sidecar test\n- [x] gate runs record request and tool-call usage durably by default, including the loop-vs-breadth axis; checked by the instrumentation child's tests\n- [x] a healthy high-breadth run is never truncated or aborted by any of the above — budgets remain failure bounds, not workload ceilings; checked by tests replaying the healthy-run profile (0.922 distinct ratio, minimum 24-window ratio 0.833) and asserting no abort\n\n## Child decomposition\n\nChildren by responsibility (dependency order): the detector signal (`distinct_ratio_window`, window 24, trip <= 0.50, single-sourced in `usage_log`) delivers criterion 5's discriminator and is a prerequisite of the actuator and the instrumentation; the protocol-safe forced landing (steering toolset replacing the empty-filter cutoff) delivers criterion 2; recovery reachability (catch extension in `CompletionAgentStep.run`) is a prerequisite of the actuator and the diagnostic surfacing; diagnostic surfacing (sidecar + close-gate message) delivers criterion 3; the actuator (typed runaway error routed to bounded recovery) delivers criterion 1; default-on usage recording delivers criterion 4.","env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","file_impact":[],"file_impact_scope":"none","keyring":[],"last_status_env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","managed_refs":[["relates_to","6c3e-67c6-eafa-45e7"]],"no_file_impact_reason":"container epic: all code impact is declared per-child (70bc, e1b1, fd84, 8b97, c827, aec1)","parent_id":null,"parent_status_uuid":"310faac1-bca5-46ce-b0c2-84d125f34d97","plan_review_phase":"execution","preconditions_summary":{"status":"pre-manifest"},"priority":1,"reverts":[],"status":"in_progress","tags":[],"ticket_id":"9b71-55b3-1bd1-4a97","ticket_type":"epic","title":"Completion gate loop breaker: detect runaways during the run, act, and land a verdict","verify_commands":[]},"source_event_uuids":["b14dd8f8-fd25-41b7-b275-1817117ba126","00df3238-15b8-4083-a0f4-ea06d8bf829c","f268d7ff-3346-4819-a806-c68a91b34128","caf8254e-e861-42aa-8c82-36e081524e2b","310faac1-bca5-46ce-b0c2-84d125f34d97","e0e92dba-1190-4d24-8f29-ebdb3f045831","5c36983a-583e-46dc-a130-1db5c82abca7","00a041cd-91c1-4f9d-8f9a-e4ced8ea8f44","319d9ae6-eef4-4ac4-b224-63d5e8f161be"]},"env_id":"ade0f2ef-51cc-45a2-bb97-c09846cd3df5","event_type":"SNAPSHOT","timestamp":1785986862645986002,"uuid":"db6462eb-e596-4f41-ae7a-babcc46fe749"}